==Trivia==
*The Japanese name of [[Countess Koryessa]] and High Countess Koryessa (コワラッキョ ''Kowarakkyo'', "Kowalakkyo") may be a combination of [[Kory]]'s Japanese name (コアラッキョ ''Koarakkyo'', "Koalakkyo") and 怖い ''kowai'' (scary).
*High Countess Koryessa, [[Archbaron Face]] and [[Grand Emperor Warumongar]] are likely based on the [[wikia:powerrangers:Growing the Monsters|Growing the Monsters]] trope from the ''[[wikipedia:Super Sentai Series|Super Sentai Series]]'', in which monsters often become giant versions of themselves on the verge of defeat.
*In the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]], High Countess Koryessa's lipstick is red, whereas in every other version it's black. She shares this trait with [[Countess Koryessa]] and [[Madam Peng]].
**This change was likely to prevent them from resembling blackface, a practice originating in American theater in which performers would heavily darken their skin and exaggerate their lips (usually via applying bright red or pink lipstick) to portray a highly offensive caricature of Africans.

